; dialect sugar + reader tests (borg/dialect.borg v0.1-v0.3).
; THE GAP THIS CLOSES: compiler_tests.exe was declared at the top of this
; file but never had a runtest rule, so `dune runtest` stayed green while
; the suite carried 4 failures -- including every `match` row, i.e. the
; whole v0.3 reader form.  A test that never runs is not a gate.  The exe
; is self-contained (no corpus on disk, unlike flat_tests), so no
; source_tree dep is needed.  The tool-language suite reads the two
; verdict sources (borg/tool-language.borg T3), hence the two files.
(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  compiler_tests.exe
  ../scripts/gate-receipts/verdict.sabra
  ../scripts/dialect/verdict-cond.sabra)
 (action
  (run %{exe:compiler_tests.exe})))

; tool-language T2 + T4 (borg/tool-language.borg): verdict-std.sabra, the
; verdict written against the seeded stdlib with pinned names, answers
; as verdict.sabra on every gate-receipt policy case; the JSON codec
; round-trips and matches the reader's literals.  No PG, no HTTP.
(executable
 (name tool_language_tests)
 (modules tool_language_tests)
 (libraries tuna tuna_interp tuna_compiler tuna_server yojson alcotest))

(rule
